ic","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/kcomponents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k-components of an undirected graph (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k ≥ 1,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the maximal sets of vertices whose induced subgraph is k-vertex-connected, that is, has more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than k vertices and stays connected after removing any k − 1 of them. The 1-components are the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"connected components with an edge, the 2-components the blocks of three or more vertices; every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"k-component lies inside a (k − 1)-component. Components at one level may share fewer than k","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"}}}